// The operator is a separate module to keep the Helm SDK and its transitive
// dependency tree out of the driver's build. The driver ships in a container
// that mounts a node's block devices; every dependency it does not have is one
// that cannot be a vulnerability there.
//
// This comment used to claim controller-runtime was excluded too. It is not,
// and saying so was worse than not saying it: the driver requires
// controller-runtime for the StorageProtectionGroup reconciler, which runs in
// the driver's controller pod because the replication manager needs appliance
// clients and those credentials exist nowhere else. The same binary serves node
// mode, so that dependency does reach the node image -- a real cost, accepted
// deliberately rather than denied. Moving the reconciler to the operator would
// remove it, at the price of the operator becoming mandatory for replication.
//
// This workspace ties the two together for local development, so an edit to the
// driver's types is seen by the operator without a replace directive or a
// tagged release. CI builds each module on its own with GOWORK=off, because
// that is what `go install` and the release build actually do.
go 1.27.0

use (
	.
	./operator
)
